        "content": [
          {
            "annotations": [],
            "text": "{\n  \"decision\": \"request_changes\",\n  \"thresholds_preserved\": true,\n  \"contradiction_requires_evidence\": true,\n  \"controls_consistent\": false,\n  \"reason\": \"The protocol preserves the stated acceptance thresholds, separates the three checks, and requires explicit conflicting text or evidence to mark a contradiction. It also appropriately distinguishes protocol completion from proven model performance and prohibits retrospective relabeling. However, the validation path says judges receive “missing-field names” without defining whether these are neutral field requirements or evaluator-derived findings about what is missing. If they encode expected omissions or unknown values, they can leak assessment labels and bias the judgments.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"issue\": \"“Missing-field names” in the judge packet are ambiguous and could expose gold-derived missingness or expected unknown values, despite the stated separation of expected labels.\",\n      \"action\": \"Define the packet contents precisely. Provide neutral required-field inventories and source evidence, but exclude any evaluator-derived list of fields judged missing, invented, or otherwise incorrect. If field names must be supplied to assess unknown-value handling, establish that they are fixed assessment inputs rather than outcome labels, and document how they are generated without using expected judgments.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
            "type": "output_text",
